# TODO - CamScanner

## Objective

Android reference; independently implement a private, offline-first document
scanner in Rust. Preserve practical scanning and document management without
requiring commercial services, subscriptions or proprietary runtime code.

## Acceptance

- Select a lawfully accessible official Android edition for behaviour
  comparisons; record its revision and observable feature scope.
- Support camera capture and image import, document edge detection,
  perspective correction, rotation, crop and readable image enhancement.
- Support multipage documents, page ordering, local OCR, search and
  export to PDF and images with user-controlled quality and storage.
- Reuse shared image processing, geometry, presentation, input, storage
  and camera capabilities. Extend the platform IR for Android camera
  access and the shared engine for reusable image processing.
- Keep captured documents, OCR text and metadata private by default.
  Bound image decoding, processing memory and PDF generation; verify
  malformed-input rejection and explicit camera permission failures.
- Provide offline operation without ads, subscription gates, cloud
  dependence or compulsory accounts. Optional sharing is user initiated.
- Verify scan quality, page ordering, save/load and export using small
  synthetic documents; do not use personal documents as test fixtures.
- Verify actual Android ARM64 behaviour; evaluate other targets through
  available platform capabilities rather than assuming camera support.
- Check lawful reference input under
  `.reference/games/camscanner/`. Never ship original app binaries,
  proprietary assets or trademarks as official branding.
- Run `cargo validate` and record remaining feature or platform limits.

## Evidence

No implementation or selected official reference revision is established.
Verify availability of lawful original media before onboarding.
